     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, which is usually given as 850 mg three times daily. The risks at this dose include lactic acidosis and severe GI intolerance. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that ceiling.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max IR dose)\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Something else**, such as an extended-release formulation (max 2,000 mg/day)\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed it. Otherwise, tell me the dose you intended and I'll enter that."
      }
     ],
